[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186133905 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-edc742b5-3b4b-536d-82ef-b613c6a8e953" "question-8779db6b-a3a9-5c0c-95e4-31a7bc1a4418" "question-c02b9ef4-844a-58b2-be01-9b59908adb2c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-edc742b5-3b4b-536d-82ef-b613c6a8e953" :question/id #uuid "edc742b5-3b4b-536d-82ef-b613c6a8e953" :question/math-academy-id "q-139577" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$-2$** | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$1$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-7$ | $-4$ | $2$ | $5$ | $10$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients  of the line $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above can be found using linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the observation vector $y$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$-2$** | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$1$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-7$ | $-4$ | $2$ | $5$ | $10$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-25a7cb9f-7a09-5793-9cb0-c7d79f0245b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-25a7cb9f-7a09-5793-9cb0-c7d79f0245b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "25a